; knowsia.com — the zone as held in Cloudflare.
;
; HISTORY. Compiled 2026-09-04 from live DNS lookups as an IMPORT draft, because
; the VPS nameservers could not answer TXT. Rewritten 2026-09-12 from
; Cloudflare's own export after the zone was created, which is now the source of
; truth — this file is a version-controlled copy, not the thing being imported.
;
; ── WHY THE MOVE WAS URGENT (still true until the registrar switch) ─────────
; Every nameserver delegated for knowsia.com is unreachable: ns1/ns2.knowsia.com
; have no A record, and ns1/ns2/ns3.noohrabusiness.com all resolve to 127.0.0.1.
; The domain resolves ONLY from stale resolver caches. Querying the VPS directly
; (64.20.36.232) answers A, NS, SOA and MX and hangs only on TXT, so the server
; is healthy and the delegation is not.
;
; ── WHAT CLOUDFLARE'S SCAN MISSED, AND IT WOULD HAVE CAUSED AN OUTAGE ───────
; The scan found 2 A, 3 CNAME, 3 MX and 10 TXT records and OMITTED
; reg.knowsia.com — live, serving 200, and the host of the registration app,
; the four portals and the 312 printed /verify/KNS-… certificate URLs.
; Switching nameservers on the scanned set would have taken all of that down.
; It also missed quiz.knowsia.com and its two TXT records.
; Cloudflare's own banner warns of this ("our scan may have missed uncommon
; records"). The lesson is the procedure: EXPORT the scanned zone and diff it
; against the live zone BEFORE touching the registrar. That diff is what caught
; this, and it cost five minutes.
;
; ── A FINDING RECORDED AS WRONG ─────────────────────────────────────────────
; This file previously asserted a DUPLICATE SPF RECORD at the apex, read off
; CyberPanel's table, and called it an RFC 7208 §4.5 PERMERROR. The founder said
; the two rows were two different zones. THE FOUNDER WAS RIGHT: Cloudflare's
; export shows exactly ONE apex SPF record. The claim is withdrawn.
; It was unfalsifiable at the time — TXT was the one record type the nameservers
; could not serve — and the right move would have been to hold the finding until
; it could be queried, not to write it up from a screenshot.
;
; ── A REAL DUPLICATE, STILL UNRESOLVED ──────────────────────────────────────
; There are TWO default._domainkey records with DIFFERENT keys, and NEITHER
; matches the key read out of CyberPanel by hand on 2026-09-12 — three distinct
; DKIM keys at one selector. Two in DNS makes verification ambiguous; the third
; was probably copied from the noohrabusiness.com zone, which lists that
; selector three times.
; ONLY CyberPanel → Email → DKIM Manager can settle it: the published record
; must match the private key the mail server signs with, and one of the two is
; stale. Until then both are left in place — deleting the live one is worse than
; the ambiguity.
;
; TTL "1" is Cloudflare's Auto. Every record is DNS-only (grey cloud): proxying
; the apex would break mail, because the MX points at the apex, and proxying
; `reg` breaks the Vercel TLS handshake.

$ORIGIN knowsia.com.

; ---------- Apex and www (TODAY: WordPress on the VPS) ----------
; Phase 3 changes these to:  @ A 76.76.21.21  and  www CNAME cname.vercel-dns.com.
@                   1  IN  A      64.20.36.232
www                 1  IN  CNAME  knowsia.com.

; ---------- Mail (on the VPS — CyberPanel / Roundcube). Must move before Phase 4 ----------
@                   1  IN  MX 10  knowsia.com.
mail                1  IN  A      64.20.36.232
mail                1  IN  MX 10  mail.knowsia.com.
@                   1  IN  TXT    "v=spf1 a mx ip4:64.20.36.232 ~all"
mail                1  IN  TXT    "v=spf1 a mx ip4:64.20.36.232 ~all"
_dmarc              1  IN  TXT    "v=DMARC1; p=none;"
_dmarc.mail         1  IN  TXT    "v=DMARC1; p=none;"

; DKIM — see "A REAL DUPLICATE" above. Two keys, one selector, unresolved.
; Recorded verbatim so the choice is auditable once DKIM Manager says which is live.
default._domainkey  1  IN  TXT    ( "v=DKIM1; h=sha256; k=rsa; "
                                    "p=MIIBIjANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQEFAAOCAQ8AMIIBCgKCAQEAzEQt082ZeZXtY8co3YELm9Proc62Xt4xJiDr7AokrVGjgJin/utOp7kU9xKTd4Soc1YJwp4TQYSkfnMs0cfZrQH4giwECAqMdLAQtxM+qfYm0j68fuEAc8jThGU22jtemHK6c1WGrz2oJAvqWDhJB2UI7pqJdfX9yLCPCUqts0FhO4QakzGy204zan1fZZp7iSNm6TM3KqS8GP"
                                    "gu+8nNrktOP1XRGy62ExZgrCXOWIRLX822U7QXW9kWHSP8U/TFUVYENCp/i61BVUynAY9E7NNDWLHzjWjup/vI+65EynGHFWxDCStU8oBdIGplUyFOkivQkBmwFha9sfmp4UajEQIDAQAB" )
default._domainkey  1  IN  TXT    ( "v=DKIM1; h=sha256; k=rsa; "
                                    "p=MIIBIjANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQEFAAOCAQ8AMIIBCgKCAQEApop6aiSox8ITkXTiJ3V+f7lEyyA4HzbdOxQTc4jm6MwPvHwYEUgRW5zFfTfLRJQ9E5edNCM60uQtowtvPB4snoTI76r3JAxlZvhKAEoUNy4MChdvXznTtVhwOxUDvj+DvZc/pFR5rlaDntfdAehzttmpFceB+Jz8T9EgamtfKD5rZtd9eomtPRKZ8RuQiI+u34y63UQNPkq1s+"
                                    "0uLWLS5qmtUOZGOMWEV0Zk+pSkmOB86/7MUWZUHZsTJuqlVxmU2MJryImQJ3mmeRgqk0f0VxB6lEw5Uj+yl2iglDGLLwZajoxbvkzgCoaImnnztFTYCHgxuWysHlFbdJcOZ2mwQQIDAQAB" )

; DELETED 2026-09-12: _domainkey  TXT  "t=y; o=~;"
; t=y is DKIM TEST MODE — it tells receivers this domain is only testing DKIM
; and not to act on failures, discarding most of the benefit. o=~ is ADSP,
; withdrawn as a standard in 2013. Do not re-add either.

; ---------- Transactional mail ----------
; Resend, via Amazon SES. Already configured before this migration, so Resend's
; DNS side is DONE — the silently-failing trial email sequence is purely the
; missing RESEND_API_KEY on Railway (KnowsiaApp PLAN.md).
send                1  IN  TXT    "v=spf1 include:amazonses.com ~all"
send                1  IN  MX 10  feedback-smtp.eu-west-1.amazonses.com.
resend._domainkey   1  IN  TXT    "p=MIGfMA0GCSqGSIb3DQEBAQUAA4GNADCBiQKBgQC4Cmhh2sAWCU3wtFjHvXF6dMxnEf2i61eDdLmWBeNrGmMM0/UFHSXuZb3LTpE1SnzM2Vz630uSnrOMGwsqD8Y7Buqk7eMmNRqWNxjK8GMDOOgMSOgSARl2V8ONNf9DO13W7ByJI/3+6WG9fZLtRrwp/HQEooPP9SHu6MTyM12xswIDAQAB"
; SMTP2GO link tracking. Was in neither the 2026-09-04 draft nor my reading of
; the panel — found only in Cloudflare's export. Keep it.
link                1  IN  CNAME  track.smtp2go.net.

; ---------- Applications ----------
; MISSING FROM CLOUDFLARE'S SCAN — added by hand 2026-09-12. See the header.
reg                 1  IN  CNAME  da623ee62209f472.vercel-dns-017.com.
; quiz.knowsia.com is BROKEN: it answers 301 to itself (a redirect loop) while
; https://knowsia-quiz-app.web.app/ is fine. A bare CNAME is not how Firebase
; Hosting custom domains work — add the domain in the Firebase console, which
; issues a TXT verification record and two anycast A records to use INSTEAD of
; this CNAME. Also missing from the scan.
quiz                1  IN  CNAME  knowsia-quiz-app.web.app.
quiz                1  IN  TXT    "hosting-site=knowsia-quiz-app"
_acme-challenge.quiz 1 IN  TXT    "NY3wQmMdbp3YUTNWZKhQh7fdeqzYHPSX-tdABbaZ160"
; Phase 1 adds:
; app               1  IN  CNAME  cname.vercel-dns.com.
; Phase 3 adds (VPS kept reachable for 60–90 days, noindex):
; legacy            1  IN  A      64.20.36.232

; ---------- Legacy hosting conveniences (VPS) ----------
ftp                 1  IN  CNAME  knowsia.com.

; ---------- Verification records ----------
; Google Search Console. The FULL token, from Cloudflare's export — CyberPanel's
; table view had truncated it at "…04H96-", and the earlier plan to abandon it
; and re-issue from a fresh Domain property is unnecessary.
@                   1  IN  TXT    "google-site-verification=UaJeCu6p0HnWs8PU04H96-mhJ0wh6678KKRNJFbkYDE"
; Vercel domain verification for knowsia.com, needed at Phase 3 (Vercel →
; course-registration → Domains shows the exact name/value when you add it):
; _vercel           1  IN  TXT    "vc-domain-verify=knowsia.com,..."

; ---------- Not carried over ----------
; ns1 / ns2.knowsia.com A records: they were glue for the self-hosted
; nameservers being abandoned, and they have no A record in the live zone
; anyway, which is half the reason the delegation is broken.
